WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.999
- What's up, y'all? We are back.

00:00:01.999 --> 00:00:04.820
And earlier I showed you a
never before seen interview

00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:06.564
with Chris Martin.

00:00:06.564 --> 00:00:08.430
We were in New York and in that same show,

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.960
SNL's Bow and Yang
stopped by to talk about

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.470
when he realized he was a true New Yorker.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.300
Here's a hint. It has to do with rats.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.480
What was there a moment that you knew

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.290
you'd become a real New Yorker,

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.420
because you're not from here, right?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.253
- I'm not from here.

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:23.086
- Okay. Where are you from?

00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:25.100
- I'm from Aurora, Colorado.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.125
- Oh, I love Colorado.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.908
- Lovely place. Colorado's
great. Colorado's great.

00:00:27.908 --> 00:00:28.817
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:32.095
- It was the town where
I cried to fix you.

00:00:32.095 --> 00:00:34.113
I was speaking to fix you.

00:00:34.113 --> 00:00:36.170
- That was Texas for me. Yes, yes.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.160
- Wonderful, wonderful.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.030
- Well, so when you, that's
very different from New York.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.420
So when you moved here, like when did you

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.790
finally feel like "I am now a New Yorker"?

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.810
- I was eating dim sum.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.200
And then I went to
Columbus Park in Chinatown,

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.990
and there was a pigeon
lady, very Home Alone Two.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:52.530
- [Kelly] Oh my god. I was
gonna say like Home Alone.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.010
- It was like, it was
a Home Alone situation,

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.198
Mary Poppins tuppence a bag.

00:00:55.198 --> 00:00:56.031
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:56.031 --> 00:01:00.030
- And then I saw a rat
scurry over her foot,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.850
and then she freaked out and screamed

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.970
and I thought, wow, this
is the most New York thing

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:04.803
I've ever seen.

00:01:04.803 --> 00:01:05.636
(audience laughs)

00:01:05.636 --> 00:01:07.410
And it's funny that like,
you're chill with pigeons,

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.580
but not chill with rats.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.057
Cause I feel like that's a package deal.

00:01:10.057 --> 00:01:11.700
- I feel like it's a flying rat.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.558
- God made them on the same
day, you know what I mean?

00:01:14.558 --> 00:01:15.748
So I don't know.

00:01:15.748 --> 00:01:18.160
- They complain about
rats in New York though,

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.760
but I'm telling you I moved to LA. Okay.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.960
And there are rats in LA.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:23.793
- Yeah, like bad rats.

00:01:23.793 --> 00:01:26.060
- That stop, look you in the eyes,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.110
let you know they're there,
and then scurry right off

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.380
and be like, I'm just going to go visit

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.100
my hundreds of family
members I am somewhere with.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.036
Like, yeah. I can't stand
rats. Anyway, whatever.

00:01:36.036 --> 00:01:38.680
So what were you? I always think this,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.050
everybody on SNL, were you like voted

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.530
class clown in high school?

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.966
Did everybody know where you were headed?

00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:46.960
- It was so the thing was,
the category was class clown,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.320
but that the title of the category was

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.720
most likely to be on
SNL, which like was just,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.440
but it was just like a
florid way of saying, oh,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.300
he's like a ham. And he's, he's.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.400
- You literally got Most
Likely to be on SNL?

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.990
- But, like, it, but in a way, like,

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.950
but back then it like
didn't mean anything to me.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.158
I was like, oh, okay, cool.

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:06.991
- What?

00:02:06.991 --> 00:02:07.950
- Because the prettiest person was like

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.890
most likely to be on the cover of a Vogue.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.120
It was like that kind of thing.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:11.953
- That's totally what I got.

00:02:11.953 --> 00:02:13.047
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:13.047 --> 00:02:13.880
(audience laughs)

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.238
- They were like, she's
going to be a model.

00:02:15.238 --> 00:02:17.600
That's, did you ever get anything?

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.640
Did you all do that where you grew up,

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.569
where you get most likely?

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:20.900
- No.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.140
- You didn't do most likelies?

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.920
- No. I think, they said my school

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.220
that I was good at lots of things,

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.470
but not that good at anything.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:28.809
(audience laughs)

00:02:28.809 --> 00:02:29.850
- A Jack of all Trades.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.570
- No, no. They said it in a nice way.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:32.837
I said I'd really liked to be a pop star.

00:02:32.837 --> 00:02:34.687
They said, well, keep dreaming.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.880
- Oh my god.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.100
- And look where we are now.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:37.933
- Lot of people told me that too, Chris.

00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:38.766
- Look at us now.

00:02:38.766 --> 00:02:39.599
- Look at us now.

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:40.432
(audience cheers)

